   "text": {
    "L1": "Food miles are the distance food travels from where it is grown or made to where it is eaten.",
    "L2": "Food miles count the whole journey, not only the trip from the shop to your home.",
    "L3": "A longer journey usually burns more fuel, adding more air pollution. Cold storage and packaging may add energy, cost and waste.",
    "L4": "Let us compare apples from Shimla with spinach from a farm near Delhi, for a family in Delhi.",
    "L5": "The apples travel about 350 kilometres, while the spinach travels about 20 kilometres. The apples go more than 15 times as far.",
    "L6": "So local and seasonal food usually travels less, is fresher and supports nearby farmers.",
    "L7": "Read labels and ask sellers where food comes from. Distance matters, but how food is grown and stored matters too.",
    "L8": "Which food used less fuel to reach the Chennai market: an apple from Himachal Pradesh or a banana from a farm 20 kilometres away?"
   },
